Begin Exploring Related Columns
Possible helpful columns and their usages

• “path”: contains the full relative pathname inside the repository – can be parsed to  
  – check the file‑extension (.py, .c, .ipynb, .java, .js)  
  – measure directory depth with REGEXP_COUNT("path", '/').  

• “repo_name”: lets you see which repository each file belongs to when you want counts per‑repo or to de‑duplicate.  

• “id”: a blob‑hash that is unique per file version – can be used if you need the exact number of unique files, irrespective of identical names.  

• “mode”, “ref”, “symlink_target”: not required for the present task.  

The key table is GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES because it lists one row per file checked into each sampled repository.  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (all limited to 20 rows) that move from simple inspection to the final aggregation step.  
All column names are double‑quoted and every query is preceded by a brief comment.

```sql
-- 1. Quick look at some file paths just to understand the data shape
SELECT "repo_name",
       "path"
FROM   GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Inspect examples whose directory depth is greater than 10
SELECT "repo_name",
       "path",
       REGEXP_COUNT("path", '/')        AS depth
FROM   GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES
WHERE  REGEXP_COUNT("path", '/') > 10
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Show a few deeply‑nested Python files
SELECT "repo_name",
       "path"
FROM   GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES
WHERE  REGEXP_COUNT("path", '/') > 10
  AND  LOWER("path") LIKE '%.py'
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Show a few deeply‑nested C source files
SELECT "repo_name",
       "path"
FROM   GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES
WHERE  REGEXP_COUNT("path", '/') > 10
  AND  LOWER("path") LIKE '%.c'
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Same idea for JavaScript files
SELECT "repo_name",
       "path"
FROM   GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES
WHERE  REGEXP_COUNT("path", '/') > 10
  AND  LOWER("path") LIKE '%.js'
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Count, per extension, how many files satisfy depth > 10
SELECT CASE
         WHEN LOWER("path") LIKE '%.py'     THEN '.py'
         WHEN LOWER("path") LIKE '%.c'      THEN '.c'
         WHEN LOWER("path") LIKE '%.ipynb'  THEN '.ipynb'
         WHEN LOWER("path") LIKE '%.java'   THEN '.java'
         WHEN LOWER("path") LIKE '%.js'     THEN '.js'
       END                             AS file_type,
       COUNT(*)                        AS file_cnt
FROM   GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES
WHERE  REGEXP_COUNT("path", '/') > 10
  AND  (
        LOWER("path") LIKE '%.py'    OR
        LOWER("path") LIKE '%.c'     OR
        LOWER("path") LIKE '%.ipynb' OR
        LOWER("path") LIKE '%.java'  OR
        LOWER("path") LIKE '%.js'
      )
GROUP  BY file_type
ORDER  BY file_cnt DESC
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Same as #6 but showing only extensions that actually occur
--    (use HAVING to filter out NULL)
SELECT file_type,
       COUNT(*) AS file_cnt
FROM  (
        SELECT CASE
                 WHEN LOWER("path") LIKE '%.py'     THEN '.py'
                 WHEN LOWER("path") LIKE '%.c'      THEN '.c'
                 WHEN LOWER("path") LIKE '%.ipynb'  THEN '.ipynb'
                 WHEN LOWER("path") LIKE '%.java'   THEN '.java'
                 WHEN LOWER("path") LIKE '%.js'     THEN '.js'
               END AS file_type
        FROM   GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES
        WHERE  REGEXP_COUNT("path", '/') > 10
      )
GROUP BY file_type
HAVING file_type IS NOT NULL
ORDER BY file_cnt DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Verify that counting by file hash ("id") gives the same ranking
SELECT file_type,
       COUNT(DISTINCT "id") AS unique_files
FROM  (
        SELECT CASE
                 WHEN LOWER("path") LIKE '%.py'     THEN '.py'
                 WHEN LOWER("path") LIKE '%.c'      THEN '.c'
                 WHEN LOWER("path") LIKE '%.ipynb'  THEN '.ipynb'
                 WHEN LOWER("path") LIKE '%.java'   THEN '.java'
                 WHEN LOWER("path") LIKE '%.js'     THEN '.js'
               END AS file_type,
               "id"
        FROM   GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES
        WHERE  REGEXP_COUNT("path", '/') > 10
      )
GROUP BY file_type
ORDER BY unique_files DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Retrieve the extension with the single highest count (depth > 10)
SELECT file_type,
       COUNT(*) AS file_cnt
FROM  (
        SELECT CASE
                 WHEN LOWER("path") LIKE '%.py'     THEN '.py'
                 WHEN LOWER("path") LIKE '%.c'      THEN '.c'
                 WHEN LOWER("path") LIKE '%.ipynb'  THEN '.ipynb'
                 WHEN LOWER("path") LIKE '%.java'   THEN '.java'
                 WHEN LOWER("path") LIKE '%.js'     THEN '.js'
               END AS file_type
        FROM   GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES
        WHERE  REGEXP_COUNT("path", '/') > 10
      )
GROUP BY file_type
ORDER BY file_cnt DESC
LIMIT 1;
```

```sql
-- 10. (Optional deeper inspection) list a few paths for whichever file type wins
SELECT "repo_name",
       "path"
FROM   GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES
WHERE  REGEXP_COUNT("path", '/') > 10
  AND  LOWER("path") LIKE '%.py'  -- replace with extension returned by query #9
LIMIT  20;
```

